{
  "schema": "ownward.organization/v1",
  "instruction": "Process each work independently, comparing its source with its listed candidates. Organize reusable connections supported by that material; shared vocabulary alone is not a relation. Create units for connected passages and their necessary context, without recataloguing the whole source. Keep distinct events, participants and conditions separate. An unsplit source uses one unit covering the whole source. Omit statement because the original passage states the fact. A mention must locate an actual occurrence, with its role; use an exact selector when its literal name is ambiguous in the unit. Each relation connects the current source to another supplied source or two of its own units. Unit and mention IDs may refer only to this work's own output or a supplied candidate inventory, never another work's output; use a raw-source selector otherwise. same_object joins two grounded mentions, never whole events. Preserve the concrete meaning and necessary conditions; record a connection once since navigation works both ways. No useful connection means empty units and links are valid. Omit empty optional fields. Return organization alongside existing semantic fields in the same call.",
